message: >-
  If you use this research repository, please cite this release using the
  metadata below. Add the Zenodo DOI to this file after DOI registration.
type: generic
title: 'Beyond the LLM Boundary: Structural Hybrid Intelligence, Representation Barriers, and the Future of AI Architecture'
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
  - name: GPT-Obot
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Beyond-the-LLM-Boundary-Structural-Hybrid-Intelligence'
url: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Beyond-the-LLM-Boundary-Structural-Hybrid-Intelligence'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A conceptual research series investigating the boundaries of language-centric
  large language models and proposing Boundary-Aware Structural Hybrid
  Intelligence (BASHI). The eight-paper framework examines computational
  representation barriers, the economics of structural specialization,
  perspective sovereignty and ownership, localization-execution decoupling,
  CCC-native structural semantic units, evidence-based governance, and
  open-ended structural intelligence growth. Its architectural and economic
  hypotheses are proposals for future empirical validation, not established
  benchmark results.
keywords:
  - structural intelligence
  - large language models
  - hybrid artificial intelligence
  - computational representation barriers
  - BASHI
  - structural localization
  - CCC-native intelligence
  - perspective sovereignty
  - AI governance
  - open-ended learning
